in half of them  we're told that they'd been on a placebo  the whole time half of them were told  that they were still on steroids the  ones who thought they were still on  steroids were able to replicate those  numbers hold onto those 10 15 kilo PRS  the ones who found out they were on  placebos the whole time in spite of the  fact that they knew that they weren't on  steroids when they hit those PRS two  weeks prior were still unable to match  them and basically went back to baseline  again just illustrating how expectations  can very strongly affect outcomes so  just to boil this down what I'm saying  is this if you want to reach your full  potential you need to start looking at  the people who are the best and expect  that you can compete on their level that  may not be within your physical limits  but until you assume that you are  capable of doing that it's simply never  going to happen  you have to us you have to play the hand  you were dealt with the assumption  that it's good enough to reach that and  see the thing is if if you don't do that  if you assume you're playing a bad hand  then when you don't make much progress  it's a lot easier to stomach so when you  expect greatness you do open yourself up  for the possibility of failure and  disappointment but you have to be  willing to do that if you're going to  reach your long-term potential so that's  it guys thanks for watching please like  and subscribe if you're interested in  reading more a lot of this was based off  of an old article I wrote that'll be  linked in the description along with  another article I wrote about steroids  largely having to do with the placebo  effect if you're interested in reading  more about that so like I said like and  subscribe thanks for watching bye
 

